# Play test of The Drowned Labyrinth (CIPlay drowned_labyrinth, in a test world 'CI ...'). Points as in its recipe: the
# dive camp on the largest islet (round -9.6 16, top ~5 m); the hole in the reef by the buoy (17 9) down to the mouth 19 m
# down; the first fork (14..23 x, -16..-5 z; its dead end east to x 33), the second fork (1..10 x) with the air bell, the
# Hall of Columns west of it (x -34..-2), the tide gate at the gate tunnel's north end (4 5) and the hole beyond it.
# Under water the steps put the player where they act (zones, chests, notes, levers).
island The Drowned Labyrinth
offset 0 0
expect step 0
expect title Forty Breaths
wait 5

# The camp: the dive plan on the chart table, a reel from the dive locker, the camp crate
walk -9 7 to -8.5 13 h=4.5
zone camp
expect step 0
read Dive leader's plan
expect step 1
open Dive locker
expect story reel 1
expect step 2
open Camp crate

# Down the hole by the buoy to the mouth; the line post - the lamps light down the tunnel; the barrel at the mouth
zone entrance
expect step 2
use linepost
expect message small lamps wake
expect shown guidelamps
expect story reel 0
open Barrel at the mouth

# The first fork: the slate; the dead end's box
read First fork slate
expect step 3
open Dead end box

# The second fork's air bell
air airbell
zone airbell
expect step 4

# The Hall of Columns: the angler, the trader's strongbox, the leader's last slate, the second air pocket
zone hall
kill Angler fish
expect step 5
open Trader's strongbox
wait 2
expect item Blueprint_Canteen 1
expect step 7
read Noor's last slate
air airbell2

# The tide gate's lever: the grate sinks, out through the gate before it shuts - and forty breaths later it shuts
use tidelever
expect message forty breaths
expect shown exitzone
zone exit
expect done
wait 42
expect message tide gate grinds shut

# The smallest islet's box under a bush
open Islet box
